# MTG logic split playbook

Applies when adding to or splitting logic under `server/src/socket/`, `server/src/state/`, or `rules-engine/src/`. Size ceiling and dual-barrel definitions live in `.cursor/rules/typescript-max-40kb-split.mdc`; the full playbook and paste prompts are in `.cursor/skills/split-ts-module/SKILL.md`.

## Where new code goes

1. Check `docs/mtg-logic-module-map.md` for the module that already owns the mechanic. Extend that module if it is under ~36KB.
2. Otherwise create a sibling in the domain's existing family: `resolution*Handlers.ts` / `resolution-handlers/`, `triggers/`, `oracleIRParser*`, `oracleIRExecutor*`.
3. For a mega parent with **no** extract family yet (`game-actions.ts`, `interaction.ts`, `ai.ts`, `applyEvent.ts`), create `<parent>-handlers/index.ts` on the first extract.

**Never** create `X/` next to `X.ts` (`socket/resolution/`, `socket/game-actions/`). The folder is `X-handlers/` — or the existing `triggers/`.

## Do not grow an oversized file

`node tools/ts-logic-file-sizes.mjs` lists everything over 40960 bytes. If the target is already over, put the new logic in a new descriptive module and import it. The parent may gain **import/re-export lines only**, and only when the same session removes more than it adds.

Also do not append to a sibling already at ~36–40KB — add a new sibling.

## Extract sequence

1. Grep a TOC of the parent (`^(export )?(async )?function`, `case ResolutionStepType`, `case '`) and note start/end lines. Do not Read the whole parent.
2. Grep the symbol for a **dual copy** in a folder submodule. If one exists, merge into the folder copy instead of creating a third.
3. Pick one self-contained cluster. If it closes over many parent helpers, extract those helpers first into a `*Utils.ts`.
4. Create the module with a header comment (origin parent, cluster, public entry symbols). Prefer `import type` for types. Add a named re-export plus a one-line comment to the folder `index.ts`.
5. Wire it: resolution uses the `resolutionHandlerDeps.ts` seam (extracted files must not import `resolution.ts`, and each extracted step type also needs pre-complete validation); other domains use parent re-export or direct leaf import. Lazy `await import(...)` is a last resort for cycles.
6. Delete the moved body from the parent.
7. Re-read changed import lines and neighbors in both files, typecheck the workspace, run targeted tests, then add the module-map row.

Move code only — no card fixes, renames, or cleanup in an extract diff.

## Session scope

One cluster per session. Stop when the new file approaches 40KB and split the cluster rather than packing more cases in. Never two writers on the same parent file.
